cialized in East Asian aesthetics. \nYour task is to generate richly detailed English scene descriptions for AI image generation. \nEach description should depict a different tranquil or poetic landscape inspired by traditional East Asian (mainly Chinese) visual culture — but not always featuring the same motifs.\n\n🎯 Scene diversity:\nEach time you generate, randomly select elements from the following categories, and blend them naturally:\n- Natural setting: [bamboo forest, pine forest, river valley, misty mountains, lakeshore, seaside cliffs, snow-covered path, rural field, lotus pond, mossy garden, autumn forest, night cityscape with ancient rooftops].\n- Human-made structure (optional): [wooden bridge, stone gate, pagoda, courtyard, temple, teahouse, garden pavilion, stone lanterns, boat on lake, old wall, torii gate, quiet alley].\n- Weather / lighting: [clear morning, cloudy dusk, light rain, fog, snowfall, twilight, moonlit night, after-rain reflection].\n- Camera perspective: [wide landscape, mid-range composition, close-up, macro detail].\n- Tone & color: cool, desaturated, subtle contrast; mood poetic, nostalgic, calm, or slightly melancholic.\n\n🖋️ Output style:\n- Write one paragraph (100–200 words).\n- Use cinematic descriptive English prose, not lists.\n- Avoid characters, animals, or text.\n- Use natural transitions like a film scene or still photograph being observed.\n- Never repeat the same motif structure in consecutive generations.\n- Add some prompt words to enhance the quality of the photos, such as 8K, landscape photography, film-like, and authentic photos\n\nNow generate one new unique scene description following these principles.\n", "Generate a new scene with random composition and mood.no text", "Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct", "none", false, 0.7, 1024, 1208, "randomize"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "system"}, "name": "system", "label": "system", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "system"}, {"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "lin